#!/usr/bin/python3
# Generated by Ask CK PyTest Creator for AWPTCM-T33234 — Port - Auto MDI/MDI-X
# Standardized ART framework script. Frame is fixed; test logic is filled per step.
#
# ==== OBJECTIVE — expected results this script must demonstrate ====
#   - Automatic MDI/MDI-X resolution on a copper link, with the pair assignment correct for
#   the cable in use — opposite roles at the two ends for a straight-through cable, and the
#   inverse resolution for a crossover cable.
#   - Automatic crossover selection in effect as the default, with the resolved MDI or MDI-X
#   role reported per port.
#   - Forced MDI and forced MDI-X settings applied and reflected in the operational state,
#   with auto restored afterwards and the port returning to an automatically resolved role.
#   - Equivalent automatic crossover resolution over a copper SFP module, including the
#   module-inserted and module-recognised states.
#   - Polarity configuration having no effect on media types that do not support it —
#   notably a fibre SFP link — reported as not applicable rather than silently applied, with
#   no change to link state.
#   - Invalid or unsupported polarity values rejected with a clear error, the port retaining
#   its prior configuration.
#   - Resolved MDI/MDI-X role re-resolving to the same role across an administrative
#   shutdown/no-shutdown cycle and a port reset, with the polarity configuration persisting.
# ==================================================================

